# Links and source freshness policy

## Links

- Link to local content with relative paths (`./03_education/README.md`, `../shared/`), not absolute filesystem paths.
- Anchors must match a real heading. GitHub slugs are lowercase, spaces become `-`, punctuation is dropped, Arabic letters are kept.
- When you rename a file or heading, update every inbound link in the same change.
- External links belong in prose only when the source is authoritative (gaca.gov.sa, official AIP publications). The weekly workflow checks them separately.

## Source freshness

Any page that makes a regulatory or operational claim carries a marker near the top:

```markdown
source-verified: 2026-11-14
```

Rules:

- The date is the day a human checked the citation against the official source, not the day the file was edited.
- Refresh the marker when the underlying GACAR part or AIP cycle changes, and when the weekly refresh task confirms the source is unchanged.
- A marker older than 180 days fails the `sources` check. Do not bump a date without doing the verification.
- `node scripts/gate.mjs` must report zero `links` and `sources` findings before a content PR is ready.
